    {
     "id": "p147.s01",
     "source": "”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p147"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p148.s01",
     "source": "Three days later the young spouse asks of her mother-in-law:"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p148"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p149.s01",
     "source": "“Tell me, mother, why do the bells sound?"
    },
    {
     "id": "p149.s02",
     "source": "Wherefore do the priests chant so low?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p149"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p150.s01",
     "source": "“’Tis nothing, daughter,” replies the elder woman."
    },
    {
     "id": "p150.s02",
     "source": "“A poor stranger who lodged here died this night.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p150"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p151.s01",
     "source": "“Ah, where is gone the Seigneur of Nann?"
    },
    {
     "id": "p151.s02",
     "source": "Mother, oh, where is he?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p151"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p152.s01",
     "source": "THE SEIGNEUR OF NANN AND THE KORRIGAN"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p152"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p153.s01",
     "source": "“He has gone to the town, my child."
    },
    {
     "id": "p153.s02",
     "source": "In a little he will come to see you.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p153"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p154.s01",
     "source": "“Ah, mother, let us speak of happy things."
    },
    {
     "id": "p154.s02",
     "source": "Must I wear my red or my blue robe at my churching?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p154"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p155.s01",
     "source": "“Neither, daughter."
    },
    {
     "id": "p155.s02",
     "source": "The mode is changed."
    },
    {
     "id": "p155.s03",
     "source": "You must wear black.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p155"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p156.s01",
     "source": "Unconscious in its art, the stream of verse carries us to the church, whence the young wife has gone to offer up thanks for the gift of children."
    },
    {
     "id": "p156.s02",
     "source": "She sees that the ancestral tomb has been opened, and a great dread is at her heart."
    },
    {
     "id": "p156.s03",
     "source": "She asks her mother-in-law who has died, and the old woman at last confesses that the Seigneur of Nann has just been buried."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p156"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p157.s01",
     "source": "That same night the young mother was interred beside her husband-lover."
    },
    {
     "id": "p157.s02",
     "source": "And the peasant folk say that from that tomb arose two saplings, the branches of which intertwined more closely as they grew."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p157"
  }
 ]
}